  "id": "quality",
  "term": "quality",
  "definition": "In this context, quality means how well a qualitative study is reported, especially how clearly, completely, and transparently its methods, findings, and ethical details are described. Higher quality reporting shows the study’s key methodological and ethical elements more fully, while lower quality reporting leaves important parts underreported.",
